A proximal alternating linearized update is any pair satisfying \[x^{k+1}\in\operatorname*{argmin}_x\left\{f(x)+\langle
abla_xH(x^k,y^k),x-x^kangle+ rac{c_k}{2}\|x-x^k\|^2ight\},\] \[y^{k+1}\in\operatorname*{argmin}_y\left\{g(y)+\langle
abla_yH(x^{k+1},y^k),y-y^kangle+ rac{d_k}{2}\|y-y^k\|^2ight\}.\] Equivalently, \[x^{k+1}\in\operatorname{prox}_{f/c_k} igl(x^k-c_k^{-1}
abla_xH(x^k,y^k) igr),\] \[y^{k+1}\in\operatorname{prox}_{g/d_k} igl(y^k-d_k^{-1}
abla_yH(x^{k+1},y^k) igr).\] Parameters must dominate the corresponding block-Lipschitz constants on the region visited when this update is used to certify KL descent.
